Body:
Can confirm this is still happening on a newer version than reported here (1.17.8) — reproduced today on 1.18.16, on Windows, so it's not something that got fixed in a recent point release.

Setup:
 - Local stdio MCP server, registered in a workspace-local opencode.json:
 {
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "mcp": {
    "my-server": {
      "type": "local",
      "command": ["node", "my-server.js"],
      "timeout": 30000
    }
  }
}
 - Started via opencode serve (not the TUI), so the discovery result can be checked directly against the HTTP API rather than inferred from the agent's behavior.

 Result:
 - GET /mcp → {"my-server":{"status":"connected"}}
 - GET /experimental/tool/ids → does not include any of the server's tools
 - GET /experimental/tool?provider=...&model=... → same, none of the server's tools appear

 So it's not just that the agent never calls the tools — OpenCode's own tool-listing endpoints never surface them either, even though the MCP status endpoint reports the server as connected. Raised the local server's timeout to 30s to rule out a slow-spawn/discovery-timeout race, no change.
 This is blocking us from using standalone local MCP servers as a tool-integration path at all right now — happy to share a minimal repro server if useful.

@YurySolovyov 
I create a [plugin](https://github.com/agentsyaml/opencode-turbo) that lets you view the current status (including editing status & tokens) in the sidebar. Although the user experience isn't great, it's better than nothing.

Try: `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json`:

```json
{
  "plugin": ["@alexsun-top/opencode-turbo@0.1.0"]
}
```

and:

`~/.config/opencode/tui.json`

```json
{
  "plugin": ["@alexsun-top/opencode-turbo@0.1.0"]
}
```
